      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i'm taking the Eurostar from London to Paris next week for a meeting. I have a couple of really heavy checked bags and i'm worried about the check in process at St Pancras. what are the specific weight/size limits for luggage and how early do i actually need to be there to get through security?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For checked luggage, the Eurostar has the following size and weight limits: checked bags weigh up to 32 kg (70 lbs) and measure 160 x 116 x 50 cm in size. You can also bring 1 piece of hand luggage on board, with a maximum weight of 16 kg (35 lbs) and size up to 55 x 40 x 25 cm. To minimize stress, it's recommended to arrive at St Pancras International airport at least 1 hour before check-in for domestic flights and 2 hours before check-in for international flights like your Paris meeting. You can then proceed to check-in, drop off your bags, collect your boarding pass, and go through security.",
